    "description": "###  Impact\r\n\r\nThe AI \"explain\" helper only checks `can_see?` on the post being explained, not its `reply_to_post`, so any authenticated user with access to the AI helper could read the raw contents of a hidden parent post by invoking \"Explain\" on a reply to it.\r\n\r\n###  Patches\r\n\r\nFixed in discourse-ai by adding `guardian.can_see?(reply_to)` before including the parent, and HTML-escapes all interpolated values).\r\n\r\n###  Workarounds\r\n\r\nDisable the AI helper \"Explain\" feature (or the AI helper entirely) until upgraded.\r\n",
